1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,500
Hi, Melbourne!

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,212
We're Group 14, Team Sweet
Potatoes, and this is POTATO —

3
00:00:05,212 --> 00:00:08,818
the Public Opinion Translation
And Tracking Outpost.

4
00:00:08,818 --> 00:00:09,922
Why POTATO?

5
00:00:09,922 --> 00:00:13,667
Because, like a sweet potato, good
ideas grow from the ground up.

6
00:00:14,367 --> 00:00:18,561
Melbourne's councils make decisions
about parks, housing and transport.

7
00:00:18,561 --> 00:00:22,854
Our fieldwork with eight international
residents found the barrier isn't a lack

8
00:00:22,854 --> 00:00:23,726
of interest.

9
00:00:23,726 --> 00:00:26,170
People can't find relevant information.

10
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:29,750
Translated policies still use
terms they don't understand.

11
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:31,826
And they don't know where
their feedback goes.

12
00:00:31,826 --> 00:00:35,036
Meanwhile, council news
arrives by mail and flyers,

13
00:00:35,036 --> 00:00:37,428
but newer residents live on Instagram.

14
00:00:38,128 --> 00:00:39,269
Meet Jason.

15
00:00:39,269 --> 00:00:43,516
He's lived in Melbourne for years,
but English isn't his first language.

16
00:00:43,516 --> 00:00:48,030
He's unhappy about a new park rule for
dogs, yet he doesn't know who to tell,

17
00:00:48,030 --> 00:00:49,320
or which words to use.

18
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:53,514
On his grocery walk, Jason
passes a POTATO post.

19
00:00:53,514 --> 00:00:56,899
Its screen shows verified
council and community notices,

20
00:00:56,899 --> 00:00:59,900
so he finds things he'd
never see in the mail.

21
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,565
Then Spud, our mascot, greets him and
lists the issues closest to this spot,

22
00:01:04,565 --> 00:01:06,775
ranked by distance and closing date.

23
00:01:07,475 --> 00:01:09,260
Jason taps the park issue.

24
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:12,292
A plain-language summary
appears in his own language,

25
00:01:12,292 --> 00:01:14,285
with difficult terms explained.

26
00:01:14,285 --> 00:01:17,366
Now he simply talks to
Spud, in his own language.

27
00:01:17,366 --> 00:01:21,085
The new park rule makes walking my dog
really inconvenient. I hope it can be

28
00:01:21,085 --> 00:01:21,941
reconsidered.

29
00:01:21,941 --> 00:01:26,644
Spud turns that into a structured
comment, original Chinese plus English,

30
00:01:26,644 --> 00:01:32,019
names the responsible department, and
lets Jason review and edit before sending.

31
00:01:32,019 --> 00:01:33,356
No audio is stored.

32
00:01:34,056 --> 00:01:36,666
Jason taps his phone on the NFC pad.

33
00:01:36,666 --> 00:01:41,108
The issue and his comment move to the
POTATO app, and the post keeps nothing.

34
00:01:41,108 --> 00:01:43,882
Tracking begins only
because Jason chose it.

35
00:01:43,882 --> 00:01:46,625
The app shows each stage:
Received, In review,

36
00:01:46,625 --> 00:01:50,363
then an outcome with a case
number, or reasons if declined.

37
00:01:50,363 --> 00:01:52,426
Notifications keep him updated.

38
00:01:53,126 --> 00:01:54,519
Not sure who to ask?

39
00:01:54,519 --> 00:01:58,898
The Q&A assistant answers from
official documents, cites its sources,

40
00:01:58,898 --> 00:02:02,355
and hands over to a named
contact when it's unsure.

41
00:02:02,355 --> 00:02:06,645
And one tap shares a card on Instagram,
so Jason's neighbours can join in.

42
00:02:07,345 --> 00:02:11,357
For Jason, that means finding
relevant issues on his everyday route,

43
00:02:11,357 --> 00:02:15,781
understanding them in his own language,
knowing which department hears him,

44
00:02:15,781 --> 00:02:17,712
and seeing what happens next.

45
00:02:17,712 --> 00:02:19,182
All without attending a meeting.

46
00:02:19,882 --> 00:02:21,330
POTATO has limits.

47
00:02:21,330 --> 00:02:25,045
Speaking in public may feel
exposing, AI can mistranslate,

48
00:02:25,045 --> 00:02:28,276
and our fieldwork didn't
include council staff.

49
00:02:28,276 --> 00:02:32,638
Next, we'll test a low-fidelity prototype
with residents across languages,

50
00:02:32,638 --> 00:02:35,998
and check whether they trust
and correct the AI's output.

51
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:40,523
POTATO: Public Opinion
Translation And Tracking Outpost.

52
00:02:40,523 --> 00:02:41,926
Voices from the ground up.
